  "id": "COMPOUND:900 - PROTEIN:1175",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between prostaglandin E2 and Neutral alpha-glucosidase AB, mediated through the drug lafutidine. Prostaglandin E2 is associated with several adverse effects, including amniotic fluid embolism, fetal heart rate abnormalities, and anaphylactoid syndrome of pregnancy, all of which are linked to lafutidine. Lafutidine, a histamine H2 receptor antagonist, is known to target Neutral alpha-glucosidase AB, which is involved in the metabolism of certain carbohydrates. The consistent association across multiple paths indicates that lafutidine may act as a bridge between prostaglandin E2 and Neutral alpha-glucosidase AB, possibly through a mechanism involving the systemic effects of prostaglandin E2 on physiological processes that are modulated by lafutidine. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact pathway remains unclear. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforces the likelihood of a biologically relevant interaction, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct role of prostaglandin E2 in this relationship.",
